  "z1122_may_ctrl": "An application MAY optionally be able to control whether a UDP checksum will be generated, but it MUST default to checksumming on.",
  "z1122_discard": "UDP MUST silently discard the datagram.",
  "z1122_recv_opt": "An application MAY optionally be able to control whether UDP datagrams without checksums should be discarded or passed to the application.",
  "z1122_controversial": "turning off UDP checksumming is very controversial.",
  "z1122_udp_optional": "Unlike the TCP checksum, the UDP checksum is optional; the value zero is transmitted in the checksum field of a UDP header to indicate the absence of a checksum.",
  "z1122_all1s": "it must transmit the checksum as all 1's (65535).",
  "z1122_tcp_never": "the TCP checksum is never optional.  The sender MUST generate it and the receiver MUST check it.",
  "z1122_tbl_off": "Sender Option to not generate checksum",
  "z1122_tbl_default": "Default is to checksum",
  "z1122_tbl_recv": "Receiver Option to require checksum",
  "z1122_ip_hdr": "A host MUST verify the IP header checksum on every received",
  "z8200_modify": "addresses from the IP header in its checksum computation must be modified for use over IPv6, to include the 128-bit IPv6 addresses instead of 32-bit IPv4 addresses.",
  "z8200_default": "the default behavior when UDP packets are originated by an IPv6 node is that the UDP checksum is not optional.",
  "z8200_must_compute": "an IPv6 node must compute a UDP checksum over the packet and the pseudo-header, and, if that computation yields a result of zero, it must be changed to hex FFFF for placement in the UDP header.",
  "z8200_discard": "IPv6 receivers must discard UDP packets containing a zero checksum and should log the error.",
  "z8200_tunnel": "protocols that use UDP as a tunnel encapsulation may enable zero-checksum mode for a specific port (or set of ports) for sending and/or receiving.",
  "z8200_6936": "Any node implementing zero-checksum mode must follow the requirements specified in \"Applicability Statement for the Use of IPv6 UDP Datagrams with Zero Checksums\" [RFC6936].",
  "z6935_update": "This specification updates IPv6 to allow a zero UDP checksum in the outer encapsulating datagram of a tunnel protocol.",
  "z6935_delete_lead": "The following text in [RFC2460], Section 8.1, fourth bullet should be deleted:",
  "z6935_quote_lead": "Unlike IPv4, when UDP packets are originated by an IPv6 node, the UDP checksum is not optional.",
  "z6935_quote_discard": "IPv6 receivers must discard UDP packets containing a zero checksum, and should log the error.",
  "z6935_repl_compute": "an IPv6 node MUST compute a UDP checksum over the packet and the pseudo-header, and, if that computation yields a result of zero, the checksum MUST be changed to hex FFFF for placement in the UDP header, as specified in [RFC2460].",
  "z6935_repl_discard": "IPv6 receivers MUST by default discard UDP packets containing a zero checksum and SHOULD log the error.",
  "z6935_repl_may": "encapsulation MAY enable zero-checksum mode for a specific port (or set of ports) for sending and/or receiving.",
  "z6935_must_follow": "implementing zero-checksum mode MUST follow the node requirements specified in Section 4 of \"Applicability Statement for the use of IPv6 UDP Datagrams with Zero Checksums\" [RFC6936].",
  "z6935_permitted": "while sending a UDP datagram with a zero checksum is permitted in",
  "z6935_unsuitable": "a zero UDP checksum is unsuitable, because it is necessary to provide the first level",
